window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["sql"]=[{"id":"sql-f0001","card":"q-sql-001-overview","sec":"sql-s001","q":"Which SQL dialect do the SQL revision examples use, and which features show it?","a":"<p>SQL Server (T-SQL). The features are <code>identity</code>, <code>top</code>, <code>#temp</code> tables, <code>ISNULL</code> and <code>PARSENAME</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0002","card":"q-sql-002-the-five-command-groups","sec":"sql-s002","q":"What are the five SQL command groups and their full names?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>DDL: Data Definition Language</li>\n  <li>DML: Data Manipulation Language</li>\n  <li>DCL: Data Control Language</li>\n  <li>TCL: Transaction Control Language</li>\n  <li>DQL: Data Query Language</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0003","card":"q-sql-002-the-five-command-groups","sec":"sql-s002","q":"What is DDL for, and which commands belong to it?","a":"<p>DDL defines the database schema in the DBMS. Its commands are <code>CREATE</code>, <code>DROP</code>, <code>ALTER</code> and <code>TRUNCATE</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0004","card":"q-sql-002-the-five-command-groups","sec":"sql-s002","q":"What is DML for, and which commands belong to it?","a":"<p>DML manipulates the data present in the database. Its commands are <code>INSERT</code>, <code>UPDATE</code> and <code>DELETE</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0005","card":"q-sql-002-the-five-command-groups","sec":"sql-s002","q":"What is DCL for, and which commands belong to it?","a":"<p>DCL handles access rights and data control. Its commands are <code>GRANT</code> and <code>REVOKE</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0006","card":"q-sql-002-the-five-command-groups","sec":"sql-s002","q":"What is TCL for, and which commands belong to it?","a":"<p>TCL handles the transactions happening in the database. Its commands are <code>COMMIT</code> and <code>ROLLBACK</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0007","card":"q-sql-002-the-five-command-groups","sec":"sql-s002","q":"What is DQL for, and which command belongs to it?","a":"<p>DQL retrieves data using SQL queries. Its command is <code>SELECT</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0008","card":"q-sql-003-create-and-use-a-database","sec":"sql-s003","q":"In SQL Server, how do you create a database called sample2 and switch to it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>create database sample2\nuse sample2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0009","card":"q-sql-004-create-a-table-with-constraints","sec":"sql-s004","q":"Which constraints does the customer table example use?","a":"<p>An identity primary key, <code>not null</code>, <code>unique</code>, <code>check</code> and <code>default</code> values.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0010","card":"q-sql-004-create-a-table-with-constraints","sec":"sql-s004","q":"How do you declare an auto-numbering primary key that starts at 1 and steps by 1?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>customerid int identity(1,1) primary key,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0011","card":"q-sql-004-create-a-table-with-constraints","sec":"sql-s004","q":"How do you make a column required, unique and limited to values above 0?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>customernumber int not null unique check (customernumber&gt;0),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0012","card":"q-sql-004-create-a-table-with-constraints","sec":"sql-s004","q":"How do you give columns default values when you create a table?","a":"<p>Use the <code>default</code> keyword in the column definition:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>areacode int default 71000,\ncountry varchar(50) default &#x27;Malaysia&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0013","card":"q-sql-005-insert-rows","sec":"sql-s005","q":"When you insert into a table with an <code>identity</code> column, what happens to that column?","a":"<p>You skip it. The values you supply start at the next column.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0014","card":"q-sql-005-insert-rows","sec":"sql-s005","q":"How do you make an insert use a column's default value?","a":"<p>Write <code>default</code> in that position of the values list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>insert into customer values\n(300,&#x27;Albert&#x27;,&#x27;John&#x27;,default,&#x27;dfdsfsdf&#x27;,default)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0015","card":"q-sql-005-insert-rows","sec":"sql-s005","q":"How do you insert several rows into <code>customer</code> in one statement, using <code>default</code> for some columns?","a":"<p>List one set of values per row, separated by commas:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>insert into customer values\n(100,&#x27;Fang Ying&#x27;,&#x27;Sham&#x27;,&#x27;418999&#x27;,&#x27;sdadasfdfd&#x27;,default),\n(200,&#x27;Mei Mei&#x27;,&#x27;Tan&#x27;,default,&#x27;adssdsadsd&#x27;,&#x27;Thailand&#x27;),\n(300,&#x27;Albert&#x27;,&#x27;John&#x27;,default,&#x27;dfdsfsdf&#x27;,default)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0016","card":"q-sql-006-display-records","sec":"sql-s006","q":"How do you display all records of a table and only particular columns?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select * from customer\nselect customerid, customernumber, lastname, firstname\nfrom customer</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0017","card":"q-sql-007-add-a-column-and-fill-it-with-update","sec":"sql-s007","q":"How do you add a new column to an existing table?","a":"<p>Use <code>alter table</code> with <code>add</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>alter table customer\nadd phonenumber varchar(20)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0018","card":"q-sql-007-add-a-column-and-fill-it-with-update","sec":"sql-s007","q":"How do you fill the new column for one specific row?","a":"<p>Use <code>update ... set ... where</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>update customer set phonenumber=&#x27;1234545346&#x27; where customerid=1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0019","card":"q-sql-008-drop-a-column-change-a-data-type","sec":"sql-s008","q":"How do you drop a column from a table?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>alter table customer\ndrop column phonenumber</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0020","card":"q-sql-008-drop-a-column-change-a-data-type","sec":"sql-s008","q":"How do you change the data type of a column?","a":"<p>Use <code>alter table</code> with <code>alter column</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>alter table customer\nalter column phonenumber varchar(10)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0021","card":"q-sql-009-delete-records-and-drop-a-table","sec":"sql-s009","q":"What happens when you run <code>delete</code> without a <code>where</code> clause?","a":"<p>It removes every record in the table.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0022","card":"q-sql-009-delete-records-and-drop-a-table","sec":"sql-s009","q":"How do you delete only the customers whose country is Thailand?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>delete\nfrom customer\nwhere country=&#x27;Thailand&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0023","card":"q-sql-009-delete-records-and-drop-a-table","sec":"sql-s009","q":"How do you drop a whole table?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>drop table customer</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0024","card":"q-sql-010-create-the-database-and-tables","sec":"sql-s010","q":"Which four tables make up the Sales Order sample database, and how are they linked?","a":"<p>The tables are customer, inventory, employee and sale. <code>sale</code> references the other three through foreign keys.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0025","card":"q-sql-010-create-the-database-and-tables","sec":"sql-s010","q":"How does the <code>sale</code> table reference the customer, inventory and employee tables?","a":"<p>With <code>references</code> on the key columns:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>CustomerID int not null references customer(CustomerID),\nInventoryID tinyint not null references Inventory(InventoryID),\nEmployeeID tinyint not null references Employee(EmployeeID),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0026","card":"q-sql-010-create-the-database-and-tables","sec":"sql-s010","q":"What data types does the <code>sale</code> table use for the date, quantity and unit price?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SaleDate date not null,\nSaleQuantity int not null,\nSaleUnitPrice smallmoney not null</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0027","card":"q-sql-010-create-the-database-and-tables","sec":"sql-s010","q":"In the SQL Sales Order database, how do you create the <code>customer</code> table?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>create table dbo.customer (\nCustomerID int NOT null primary key,\nCustomerFirstName varchar(50) NOT null,\nCustomerLastName varchar(50) NOT null,\nCustomerAddress varchar(50) NOT null,\nCustomerSuburb varchar(50) null,\nCustomerCity varchar(50) NOT null,\nCustomerPostCode char(4) null,\nCustomerPhoneNumber char(12) null\n);</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0028","card":"q-sql-010-create-the-database-and-tables","sec":"sql-s010","q":"In the SQL Sales Order database, how do you create the <code>inventory</code> table?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>create table dbo.inventory (\nInventoryID tinyint NOT null primary key,\nInventoryName varchar(50) NOT null,\nInventoryDescription varchar(255) null\n);</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0029","card":"q-sql-010-create-the-database-and-tables","sec":"sql-s010","q":"In the SQL Sales Order database, how do you create the <code>employee</code> table?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>create table dbo.employee (\nEmployeeID tinyint NOT null primary key,\nEmployeeFirstName varchar(50) NOT null,\nEmployeeLastName varchar(50) NOT null,\nEmployeeExtension char(4) null\n);</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0030","card":"q-sql-010-create-the-database-and-tables","sec":"sql-s010","q":"How do you create and switch to the SaleOrder database in SQL Server?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>create database SaleOrder\nuse SaleOrder</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0031","card":"q-sql-011-check-which-tables-exist","sec":"sql-s011","q":"How do you list the tables that exist in a SQL Server database?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select * from information_schema.tables</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0032","card":"q-sql-012-top-order-by-and-distinct","sec":"sql-s012","q":"How do you show only the first two rows of a table in SQL Server?","a":"<p>Use <code>top 2</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select top 2 * from customer</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0033","card":"q-sql-012-top-order-by-and-distinct","sec":"sql-s012","q":"How do you return a percentage of the rows with <code>top</code>?","a":"<p>Use <code>top n percent</code>. <code>top 40 percent</code> also gives two rows on the sample customer table.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select top 40 percent * from customer</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0034","card":"q-sql-012-top-order-by-and-distinct","sec":"sql-s012","q":"What is the default sort direction of <code>order by</code>, and how do you reverse it?","a":"<p>Ascending is the default. Add <code>desc</code> to sort descending.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>order by customerlastname desc</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0035","card":"q-sql-012-top-order-by-and-distinct","sec":"sql-s012","q":"Can <code>order by</code> use column positions instead of names?","a":"<p>Yes. It accepts column numbers.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>order by 4, 2, 3 desc</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0036","card":"q-sql-012-top-order-by-and-distinct","sec":"sql-s012","q":"What does <code>distinct</code> do?","a":"<p>It returns unique values only.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select distinct customerlastname from customer\norder by customerlastname</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0037","card":"q-sql-013-save-a-result-into-another-table","sec":"sql-s013","q":"How do you store a query result in a new table?","a":"<p>Use <code>into</code>. It creates a new base table and keeps the data types.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select distinct customerlastname into temp\nfrom customer\norder by customerlastname</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0038","card":"q-sql-014-like-and-in","sec":"sql-s014","q":"In a <code>like</code> pattern, what does <code>_</code> match and what does <code>%</code> match?","a":"<p><code>_</code> matches exactly one character. <code>%</code> matches zero, one or many characters.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0039","card":"q-sql-014-like-and-in","sec":"sql-s014","q":"What does <code>like '_r%'</code> match?","a":"<p>Values whose second character is <code>r</code>, because <code>_</code> is one character and <code>%</code> is anything after it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>where customerlastname like &#x27;_r%&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0040","card":"q-sql-014-like-and-in","sec":"sql-s014","q":"How do you search for several values in one condition?","a":"<p>Use <code>in</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>where customerlastname in (&#x27;Brown&#x27;, &#x27;Michael&#x27;, &#x27;Jim&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0041","card":"q-sql-015-comparison-operators-and-null-checks","sec":"sql-s015","q":"How do you filter for last names that are not 'Brown'?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>where customerlastname &lt;&gt; &#x27;Brown&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0042","card":"q-sql-015-comparison-operators-and-null-checks","sec":"sql-s015","q":"How do you find rows where a column is NULL, and rows where it is not?","a":"<p>Use <code>IS NULL</code> and <code>IS NOT NULL</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>where customerlastname IS NULL\nwhere customerlastname IS NOT NULL</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0043","card":"q-sql-015-comparison-operators-and-null-checks","sec":"sql-s015","q":"How do you compare a text column with a value using <code>&gt;</code> and <code>or</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>where customerlastname &gt; &#x27;Brown&#x27; or customerlastname &gt; &#x27;Cross&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0044","card":"q-sql-016-between","sec":"sql-s016","q":"How do you select sales whose unit price is from 5 to 10?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select * from sale\nwhere saleunitprice between 5 and 10</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0045","card":"q-sql-017-count-and-aliases","sec":"sql-s017","q":"What does <code>count(*)</code> return?","a":"<p>The number of rows.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0046","card":"q-sql-017-count-and-aliases","sec":"sql-s017","q":"What does <code>AS</code> do?","a":"<p>It gives a column or table a temporary name (an alias).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0047","card":"q-sql-017-count-and-aliases","sec":"sql-s017","q":"How do you count customers whose first name starts with B and name the result column \"Number of Records\"?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select count(*) as [Number of Records] from customer\nwhere customerfirstname like &#x27;B%&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0048","card":"q-sql-018-sum-with-group-by","sec":"sql-s018","q":"How do you get each employee's number of orders and total quantity?","a":"<p>Join sale to employee, then group by the employee columns:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select sale.employeeid, EmployeeFirstName, EmployeeLastName,\ncount(*) as [Number of order],\nsum(salequantity) as [Total Quantity]\nfrom sale, employee\nwhere sale.employeeid = employee.employeeid\ngroup by sale.employeeid, EmployeeFirstName, EmployeeLastName</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0049","card":"q-sql-019-group-by-month","sec":"sql-s019","q":"How do you group sales by month and show the count and total amount?","a":"<p>Group by <code>month(saledate)</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select month(saledate) as [Month], count(*) as [Number of sale],\nsum(salequantity*saleunitprice) as [Total Amount]\nfrom sale\ngroup by month(saledate)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0050","card":"q-sql-020-max-min-and-avg","sec":"sql-s020","q":"How do you get the highest, lowest and average salary?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT MAX(Salary) FROM EmployeeSalary\nSELECT MIN(Salary) FROM EmployeeSalary\nSELECT AVG(Salary) FROM EmployeeSalary</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0051","card":"q-sql-021-having","sec":"sql-s021","q":"What does <code>having</code> do?","a":"<p>It filters groups after aggregation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0052","card":"q-sql-021-having","sec":"sql-s021","q":"How do you list job titles that occur more than once?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT JobTitle, COUNT(JobTitle)\nFROM EmployeeDemographics ED\nJOIN EmployeeSalary ES\nON ED.EmployeeID = ES.EmployeeID\nGROUP BY JobTitle\nHAVING COUNT(JobTitle) &gt; 1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0053","card":"q-sql-021-having","sec":"sql-s021","q":"How do you list job titles with an average salary above 45000, sorted by that average?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>GROUP BY JobTitle\nHAVING AVG(Salary) &gt; 45000\nORDER BY AVG(Salary)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0054","card":"q-sql-022-cast-and-convert","sec":"sql-s022","q":"What do <code>CAST</code> and <code>CONVERT</code> do?","a":"<p>Both change a data type for use in the query only.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0055","card":"q-sql-022-cast-and-convert","sec":"sql-s022","q":"What is the syntax of <code>CAST</code>, and how do you cast a string to a date?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>-- CAST(expression AS datatype(length))\nSELECT CAST(&#x27;2017-08-25 00:00:00.000&#x27; AS date)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0056","card":"q-sql-022-cast-and-convert","sec":"sql-s022","q":"What is the syntax of <code>CONVERT</code>, and how do you convert a string to a date?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>-- CONVERT(data_type(length), expression, style)\nSELECT CONVERT(date,&#x27;2017-08-25 00:00:00.000&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0057","card":"q-sql-023-case-statement","sec":"sql-s023","q":"How do you label people as Old, Young or Baby by age with <code>CASE</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>CASE\nWHEN Age &gt; 30 THEN &#x27;Old&#x27;\nWHEN Age BETWEEN 27 AND 30 THEN &#x27;Young&#x27;\nELSE &#x27;Baby&#x27;\nEND</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0058","card":"q-sql-023-case-statement","sec":"sql-s023","q":"How do you show only employees with a known age, sorted by age, with the <code>CASE</code> label?","a":"<p>Add <code>WHERE Age IS NOT NULL</code> and <code>ORDER BY Age</code> after the <code>FROM</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>FROM EmployeeDemographics ED\nWHERE Age IS NOT NULL\nORDER BY Age</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0059","card":"q-sql-023-case-statement","sec":"sql-s023","q":"How can <code>CASE</code> compute values, such as a raise by job title?","a":"<p>Put an expression after <code>THEN</code> and name the result with <code>AS</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>CASE\nWHEN JobTitle = &#x27;Salesman&#x27; THEN Salary + (Salary *.10)\nWHEN JobTitle = &#x27;Accountant&#x27; THEN Salary + (Salary *.05)\nWHEN JobTitle = &#x27;HR&#x27; THEN Salary + (Salary *.000001)\nELSE Salary + (Salary *.03)\nEND AS SalaryAfterRaise</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0060","card":"q-sql-024-partition-by","sec":"sql-s024","q":"What is the difference between <code>GROUP BY</code> and <code>OVER (PARTITION BY ...)</code>?","a":"<p><code>GROUP BY</code> collapses rows. <code>OVER (PARTITION BY ...)</code> returns a single value for each row while still showing the detail columns.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0061","card":"q-sql-024-partition-by","sec":"sql-s024","q":"How do you show each employee together with the count of people of the same gender?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>COUNT(Gender) OVER (PARTITION BY Gender) AS TotalGender</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0062","card":"q-sql-025-string-functions-trim-and-replace","sec":"sql-s025","q":"Which functions remove spaces from a string?","a":"<p><code>TRIM</code>, <code>RTRIM</code> and <code>LTRIM</code> remove spaces from a string.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Select EmployeeID, TRIM(EmployeeID) AS IDTRIM\nSelect EmployeeID, RTRIM(EmployeeID) as IDRTRIM\nSelect EmployeeID, LTRIM(EmployeeID) as IDLTRIM</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0063","card":"q-sql-025-string-functions-trim-and-replace","sec":"sql-s025","q":"How do you remove the text '- Fired' from a last name?","a":"<p>Replace it with an empty string:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Select LastName, REPLACE(LastName, &#x27;- Fired&#x27;, &#x27;&#x27;) as LastNameFixed\nFROM EmployeeErrors</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0064","card":"q-sql-026-string-functions-substring-upper-and-low","sec":"sql-s026","q":"How do you take the first three characters of a first name?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Select Substring(err.FirstName,1,3), Substring(dem.FirstName,1,3),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0065","card":"q-sql-026-string-functions-substring-upper-and-low","sec":"sql-s026","q":"How do you match two tables on the first three letters of first and last names?","a":"<p>Use <code>Substring</code> in the join condition:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on Substring(err.FirstName,1,3) = Substring(dem.FirstName,1,3)\nand Substring(err.LastName,1,3) = Substring(dem.LastName,1,3)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0066","card":"q-sql-026-string-functions-substring-upper-and-low","sec":"sql-s026","q":"How do you convert a name to lower case and to upper case?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Select firstname, LOWER(firstname)\nfrom EmployeeErrors\nSelect Firstname, UPPER(FirstName)\nfrom EmployeeErrors</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0067","card":"q-sql-027-create-and-run-a-stored-procedure","sec":"sql-s027","q":"What does the Temp_Employee stored procedure take, and what does it do?","a":"<p>It takes a <code>@JobTitle</code> parameter, fills a temp table for that job title, and returns it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0068","card":"q-sql-027-create-and-run-a-stored-procedure","sec":"sql-s027","q":"How do you declare a stored procedure with a parameter in T-SQL?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>CREATE PROCEDURE Temp_Employee\n@JobTitle nvarchar(100)\nAS</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0069","card":"q-sql-027-create-and-run-a-stored-procedure","sec":"sql-s027","q":"How do you run the Temp_Employee stored procedure for Salesman?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>EXEC Temp_Employee @JobTitle = &#x27;Salesman&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0070","card":"q-sql-027-create-and-run-a-stored-procedure","sec":"sql-s027","q":"After a stored procedure is created, which line do you need on later runs?","a":"<p>Only the <code>EXEC</code> line.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0071","card":"q-sql-027-create-and-run-a-stored-procedure","sec":"sql-s027","q":"How does the stored procedure avoid an error if its temp table already exists?","a":"<p>It starts with a drop-if-exists line:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>DROP TABLE IF EXISTS #temp_employee</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0072","card":"q-sql-028-subquery-in-select-and-with-partition-by","sec":"sql-s028","q":"How do you show each salary next to the average of all salaries using a subquery in <code>SELECT</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT EmployeeID, Salary,\n(SELECT AVG(Salary) FROM EmployeeSalary) AS AllAvgSalary\nFROM EmployeeSalary</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0073","card":"q-sql-028-subquery-in-select-and-with-partition-by","sec":"sql-s028","q":"How do you get the same result with <code>PARTITION BY</code> instead of a subquery?","a":"<p>Use an empty <code>OVER ()</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT EmployeeID, Salary, AVG(Salary) OVER () AS AllAvgSalary\nFROM EmployeeSalary</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0074","card":"q-sql-029-subquery-in-from","sec":"sql-s029","q":"How do you use a subquery in the <code>FROM</code> clause?","a":"<p>Wrap it in parentheses and give it an alias:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT a.EmployeeID, AllAvgSalary\nFROM (SELECT EmployeeID, Salary, AVG(Salary) OVER () AS AllAvgSalary\nFROM EmployeeSalary) a\nORDER BY a.EmployeeID</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0075","card":"q-sql-030-subquery-in-where","sec":"sql-s030","q":"How do you select salaries of employees older than 30 using a subquery in <code>WHERE</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT EmployeeID, JobTitle, Salary\nFROM EmployeeSalary\nWHERE EmployeeID in (SELECT EmployeeID FROM EmployeeDemographics\nWHERE Age &gt; 30)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0076","card":"q-sql-030-subquery-in-where","sec":"sql-s030","q":"How do you find the employees with the highest salary using a subquery?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT EmployeeID, JobTitle, Salary\nFROM EmployeeSalary\nWHERE Salary in (SELECT Max(Salary) FROM EmployeeSalary)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0077","card":"q-sql-031-join-types","sec":"sql-s031","q":"What join types does SQL have?","a":"<p>Inner join, self join, outer join (left, right, full) and cross join.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0078","card":"q-sql-032-explicit-join-comma-syntax-no-join-keywo","sec":"sql-s032","q":"How do you join two tables without the <code>JOIN</code> keyword?","a":"<p>List both tables after <code>from</code> and match them in <code>where</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select * from inventory, sale\nwhere sale.inventoryid=inventory.inventoryid</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0079","card":"q-sql-032-explicit-join-comma-syntax-no-join-keywo","sec":"sql-s032","q":"How do you compute a total amount per sale with the comma join syntax?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select inventoryname, saledate, saleunitprice, salequantity,\nsalequantity*saleunitprice as [Total amount]\nfrom sale, inventory\nwhere sale.inventoryid=inventory.inventoryid</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0080","card":"q-sql-033-inner-join-join-keyword","sec":"sql-s033","q":"How do you write an inner join with the <code>JOIN</code> keyword?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select * from inventory\ninner join sale\non sale.inventoryid=inventory.inventoryid</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0081","card":"q-sql-033-inner-join-join-keyword","sec":"sql-s033","q":"How do you list inventory name, sale date and total amount using an inner join, sorted by inventory name?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select inventoryname, saledate, saleunitprice, salequantity,\nsaleunitprice*salequantity as [Total Amount]\nfrom inventory inner join sale\non sale.inventoryid=inventory.inventoryid\norder by inventoryname</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0082","card":"q-sql-034-left-join","sec":"sql-s034","q":"What does a left join return?","a":"<p>It keeps every row of the left table (inventory). Rows with no sales get NULL.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select inventory.inventoryid, inventoryname\nfrom inventory left join sale on\nsale.inventoryid=inventory.inventoryid</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0083","card":"q-sql-034-left-join","sec":"sql-s034","q":"How do you find inventory that never sold using a left join?","a":"<p>Add <code>where sale.inventoryid is NULL</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>where sale.inventoryid is NULL</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0084","card":"q-sql-034-left-join","sec":"sql-s034","q":"How do you find inventory with no sales without a join?","a":"<p>Use a subquery with <code>not in</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select inventoryid, inventoryname from inventory\nwhere inventoryid not in (select inventoryid from sale)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0085","card":"q-sql-035-right-join-and-full-outer-join","sec":"sql-s035","q":"How do you write a right join between inventory and sale?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select sale.inventoryid, inventoryname\nfrom inventory right join sale on\nsale.inventoryid=inventory.inventoryid</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0086","card":"q-sql-035-right-join-and-full-outer-join","sec":"sql-s035","q":"How do you write a full outer join, and how do you keep only inventory with no sales?","a":"<p>A full outer join shows everything. The <code>where</code> clause keeps inventory with no sales.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from inventory\nfull outer join sale on\nsale.inventoryid=inventory.inventoryid\nwhere sale.inventoryid is NULL</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0087","card":"q-sql-036-self-join","sec":"sql-s036","q":"What is a self join commonly used for?","a":"<p>Processing hierarchies, such as employees and their managers in one staff table.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0088","card":"q-sql-036-self-join","sec":"sql-s036","q":"How do you write a self join to show each employee with the manager's name?","a":"<p>Join the staff table to itself with two aliases:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select E.employeeID,\nE.employeefirstname+&#x27; &#x27;+E.employeelastname as [Full Name],\nE.managerID,\nM.employeefirstname+&#x27; &#x27;+M.employeelastname as [Manager Name]\nfrom staff E\ninner join staff M\non E.managerID = M.employeeID</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0089","card":"q-sql-036-self-join","sec":"sql-s036","q":"With an inner self join on the staff table, why does the top manager disappear from the result?","a":"<p>The top manager (Tan Mei Ling, 1001) has a NULL managerID, so there is no manager row to match. The result has only Kelvin Koh (manager Tan Mei Ling) and Amin Wong (manager Kelvin Koh).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0090","card":"q-sql-037-self-join-with-left-outer-join","sec":"sql-s037","q":"How do you list all employees in a self join, including the one with no manager?","a":"<p>Use a left outer join:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from staff E\nleft outer join staff M\non E.managerID = M.employeeID</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0091","card":"q-sql-037-self-join-with-left-outer-join","sec":"sql-s037","q":"What does the left outer self join on the staff table show for employee 1001?","a":"<p>Tan Mei Ling appears with an empty managerID and an empty manager name. Employees 1002 and 1003 show their managers, Tan Mei Ling and Kelvin Koh.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0092","card":"q-sql-038-cross-join","sec":"sql-s038","q":"What does a cross join do?","a":"<p>It generates every combination of records (a Cartesian product).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0093","card":"q-sql-038-cross-join","sec":"sql-s038","q":"How do you write a cross join of two inventory tables?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select * from inventory1\ncross join inventory2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0094","card":"q-sql-039-union-and-union-all","sec":"sql-s039","q":"What must match when you combine two tables with a set operator?","a":"<p>The number of columns and each column's data type. No common key is needed, only common attributes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0095","card":"q-sql-039-union-and-union-all","sec":"sql-s039","q":"UNION vs UNION ALL?","a":"<p><code>union</code> merges and hides duplicate records. <code>union all</code> merges and shows everything, duplicates included.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0096","card":"q-sql-039-union-and-union-all","sec":"sql-s039","q":"How do you write <code>union</code> and <code>union all</code> on two customer tables?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select cust_lname, cust_fname from customer\nunion\nselect cust_lname, cust_fname from customer_2\n\nselect cust_lname, cust_fname from customer\nunion all\nselect cust_lname, cust_fname from customer_2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0097","card":"q-sql-040-intersect","sec":"sql-s040","q":"What does <code>intersect</code> return?","a":"<p>Only rows common to both queries, without duplicates.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select cust_lname, cust_fname from customer\nintersect\nselect cust_lname, cust_fname from customer_2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0098","card":"q-sql-040-intersect","sec":"sql-s040","q":"How can you get the same result as <code>intersect</code> with a join condition?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select c.cust_lname, c.cust_fname from customer c, customer_2 c2\nwhere c.cust_lname=c2.cust_lname and c.cust_fname=c2.cust_fname</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0099","card":"q-sql-041-except","sec":"sql-s041","q":"What does <code>except</code> return?","a":"<p>Only the records unique to the first table (customer).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select cust_lname, cust_fname from customer\nexcept\nselect cust_lname, cust_fname from customer_2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0100","card":"q-sql-041-except","sec":"sql-s041","q":"How can you get the same result as <code>except</code> with a subquery?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select cust_lname, cust_fname from customer\nwhere (cust_lname) not in (select cust_lname from customer_2)\nand (cust_fname) not in (select cust_fname from customer_2)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0101","card":"q-sql-042-view","sec":"sql-s042","q":"What is a view?","a":"<p>The result set of a SQL statement. It is not stored data, and it is updated when the base tables are updated.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0102","card":"q-sql-042-view","sec":"sql-s042","q":"How do you create a view of customer sales?","a":"<p>Use <code>create view ... as</code> followed by the query:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>create view CustomerView as\nselect customerfirstname+&#x27; &#x27;+customerlastname as [Customer Name],\ncustomerphonenumber,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0103","card":"q-sql-043-temp-table","sec":"sql-s043","q":"How do you recognize a temp table in SQL Server, and where is it created?","a":"<p>Its name starts with a single <code>#</code>. It is physically created in the Tempdb database.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0104","card":"q-sql-043-temp-table","sec":"sql-s043","q":"What can you do with a temp table, and does it follow changes in the base table?","a":"<p>It supports CRUD, joins and other operations like a persistent table. It is not updated when the base table changes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0105","card":"q-sql-043-temp-table","sec":"sql-s043","q":"How do you create a temp table safely and fill it from a query?","a":"<p>Drop it if it exists, create it, then insert:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>DROP TABLE IF EXISTS #temp_Employee\nCreate table #temp_Employee (\nJobTitle varchar(100),\nEmployeesPerJob int,\nAvgAge int,\nAvgSalary int\n)\nInsert INTO #temp_Employee</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0106","card":"q-sql-044-cte-common-table-expression","sec":"sql-s044","q":"What is a CTE?","a":"<p>A temporary result set used to handle complex subqueries.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0107","card":"q-sql-044-cte-common-table-expression","sec":"sql-s044","q":"Where is a CTE created, and what does that mean for indexes?","a":"<p>It is created in memory, not in Tempdb, so no index can be created on it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0108","card":"q-sql-044-cte-common-table-expression","sec":"sql-s044","q":"How do you define and query a CTE?","a":"<p>Define it with <code>WITH ... AS</code>, then select from it:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>WITH CTE_Employee AS\n(\nSELECT FirstName, LastName, Gender, Salary,\nCOUNT(Gender) OVER (PARTITION BY Gender) AS TotalGender\nFROM EmployeeDemographics ED\nJOIN EmployeeSalary ES\nON ED.EmployeeID = ES.EmployeeID\nWHERE Salary &gt; &#x27;45000&#x27;\n)\nSELECT FirstName, LastName, Gender, TotalGender\nFROM CTE_Employee\nWHERE TotalGender = (SELECT MIN(TotalGender) FROM CTE_Employee)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0109","card":"q-sql-045-duplicate-a-table","sec":"sql-s045","q":"How do you copy a query result of customers, sales and inventory into a new table called customerRec?","a":"<p>Put <code>into customerRec</code> in the select list:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>salequantity*saleunitprice as [Total Amount] into customerRec\nfrom customer inner join sale on customer.customerid=sale.customerid\ninner join inventory\non sale.inventoryid=inventory.inventoryid\norder by customerfirstname+&#x27; &#x27;+customerlastname, inventoryname</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0110","card":"q-sql-046-row-number","sec":"sql-s046","q":"What does <code>ROW_NUMBER</code> do with rows that have similar values?","a":"<p>It gives a unique sequential number to each row, so similar values still get different numbers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0111","card":"q-sql-046-row-number","sec":"sql-s046","q":"How do you rank employees by salary, highest first, with <code>ROW_NUMBER</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT *,\nROW_NUMBER() OVER(ORDER BY Salary DESC) SalaryRank\nFROM EmployeeSalary</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0112","card":"q-sql-047-rank","sec":"sql-s047","q":"How does <code>RANK</code> treat rows with similar values?","a":"<p>It gives them the same rank, then skips the next rank.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0113","card":"q-sql-047-rank","sec":"sql-s047","q":"How do you rank salaries without and with <code>PARTITION BY</code>, and what does <code>PARTITION BY</code> change?","a":"<p><code>PARTITION BY</code> ranks each group separately.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>RANK() OVER(ORDER BY Salary DESC) SalaryRank\nRANK() OVER(PARTITION BY JobTitle ORDER BY Salary DESC) SalaryRank</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0114","card":"q-sql-048-dense-rank","sec":"sql-s048","q":"RANK vs DENSE_RANK?","a":"<p>Both give duplicates the same rank. <code>RANK</code> skips the next rank after duplicates. <code>DENSE_RANK</code> keeps the sequence with no gap.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0115","card":"q-sql-048-dense-rank","sec":"sql-s048","q":"How do you rank all employees by salary, highest first, with <code>DENSE_RANK</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT *,\nDENSE_RANK() OVER(ORDER BY Salary DESC) SalaryRank\nFROM EmployeeSalary\nORDER BY SalaryRank</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0116","card":"q-sql-048-dense-rank","sec":"sql-s048","q":"How do you write <code>DENSE_RANK</code> per job title?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>DENSE_RANK() OVER(PARTITION BY JobTitle ORDER BY Salary DESC) SalaryRank</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0117","card":"q-sql-049-ntile","sec":"sql-s049","q":"What does <code>NTILE(n)</code> do?","a":"<p>It splits the result into n groups and numbers each row by its group.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0118","card":"q-sql-049-ntile","sec":"sql-s049","q":"How do you split salaries into three groups, overall and per job title?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>NTILE(3) OVER(ORDER BY Salary DESC) SalaryRank\nNTILE(3) OVER(PARTITION BY JobTitle ORDER BY Salary DESC) SalaryRank</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0119","card":"q-sql-050-invoices-for-customers-with-a-balance-of","sec":"sql-s050","q":"How do you show invoice number, customer number, customer name, invoice date and amount for customers with a balance of 1000 or more, using the comma join?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select invoice_num, c.cust_num, c.cust_lname, c.cust_fname, inv_date, inv_amount\nfrom customer c, invoice\nwhere c.cust_num=invoice.cust_num and cust_balance&gt;=1000</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0120","card":"q-sql-050-invoices-for-customers-with-a-balance-of","sec":"sql-s050","q":"How do you write the same invoice query with <code>join</code> and a combined name column?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>select invoice_num, c.cust_num, cust_lname+&#x27; &#x27;+cust_fname as [Name],\ninv_date, inv_amount\nfrom customer c join invoice i\non c.cust_num=i.cust_num\nwhere cust_balance&gt;=1000</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0121","card":"q-sql-051-fill-null-values-with-isnull","sec":"sql-s051","q":"What does <code>ISNULL(expression, value)</code> return?","a":"<p>It returns <code>value</code> when <code>expression</code> is NULL.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0122","card":"q-sql-051-fill-null-values-with-isnull","sec":"sql-s051","q":"Why can you fill a missing PropertyAddress from another row with the same ParcelID?","a":"<p>When the ParcelID is the same but the UniqueID differs, the property address can be assumed to be the same.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0123","card":"q-sql-051-fill-null-values-with-isnull","sec":"sql-s051","q":"How do you find rows with a NULL PropertyAddress and their fill-in value from a matching ParcelID?","a":"<p>Self join on ParcelID with different UniqueID:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Select a.ParcelID, a.PropertyAddress, b.ParcelID, b.PropertyAddress,\nISNULL(a.PropertyAddress,b.PropertyAddress)\nFrom NashvilleHousing a\nJOIN NashvilleHousing b\non a.ParcelID = b.ParcelID\nAND a.[UniqueID] &lt;&gt; b.[UniqueID]\nWhere a.PropertyAddress is null</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0124","card":"q-sql-051-fill-null-values-with-isnull","sec":"sql-s051","q":"How do you update the NULL PropertyAddress values with the filled value?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Update a\nSET PropertyAddress = ISNULL(a.PropertyAddress,b.PropertyAddress)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0125","card":"q-sql-052-split-a-column-by-delimiter","sec":"sql-s052","q":"Which functions split PropertyAddress into address and city, and what do they do?","a":"<p><code>SUBSTRING(string, start, length)</code>, <code>CHARINDEX(substring, string, start)</code> and <code>LEN(string)</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0126","card":"q-sql-052-split-a-column-by-delimiter","sec":"sql-s052","q":"How do you take the part of PropertyAddress before the comma, and the part after it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SUBSTRING(PropertyAddress, 1, CHARINDEX(&#x27;,&#x27;, PropertyAddress) -1 ) as Address,\nSUBSTRING(PropertyAddress, CHARINDEX(&#x27;,&#x27;, PropertyAddress) + 1, LEN(PropertyAddress)) as City</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0127","card":"q-sql-052-split-a-column-by-delimiter","sec":"sql-s052","q":"How do you save the split address into new columns?","a":"<p>Add the columns with <code>ALTER TABLE</code>, then fill them with <code>Update</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ALTER TABLE NashvilleHousing\nAdd PropertySplitAddress Nvarchar(255);\nUpdate NashvilleHousing\nSET PropertySplitAddress = SUBSTRING(PropertyAddress, 1, CHARINDEX(&#x27;,&#x27;, PropertyAddress) -1 )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0128","card":"q-sql-053-split-a-column-with-parsename","sec":"sql-s053","q":"What does <code>PARSENAME('object_name', object_piece)</code> do, and in which order does it number the pieces?","a":"<p>It returns one piece of a dot-separated name. Pieces are numbered from right to left.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0129","card":"q-sql-053-split-a-column-with-parsename","sec":"sql-s053","q":"Why do you use <code>REPLACE</code> with <code>PARSENAME</code> to split a comma-separated address?","a":"<p><code>PARSENAME</code> splits on <code>.</code>, so <code>REPLACE</code> turns the commas into dots first.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0130","card":"q-sql-053-split-a-column-with-parsename","sec":"sql-s053","q":"How do you split OwnerAddress into three parts with <code>PARSENAME</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Select OwnerAddress,\nPARSENAME(REPLACE(OwnerAddress, &#x27;,&#x27;, &#x27;.&#x27;) , 3),\nPARSENAME(REPLACE(OwnerAddress, &#x27;,&#x27;, &#x27;.&#x27;) , 2),\nPARSENAME(REPLACE(OwnerAddress, &#x27;,&#x27;, &#x27;.&#x27;) , 1)\nFrom NashvilleHousing</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0131","card":"q-sql-053-split-a-column-with-parsename","sec":"sql-s053","q":"How do you store the split OwnerAddress street and city in new columns?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ALTER TABLE NashvilleHousing\nAdd OwnerSplitAddress Nvarchar(255);\nALTER TABLE NashvilleHousing\nAdd OwnerSplitCity Nvarchar(255);\nUpdate NashvilleHousing\nSET OwnerSplitAddress = PARSENAME(REPLACE(OwnerAddress, &#x27;,&#x27;, &#x27;.&#x27;) , 3)\nUpdate NashvilleHousing\nSET OwnerSplitCity = PARSENAME(REPLACE(OwnerAddress, &#x27;,&#x27;, &#x27;.&#x27;) , 2)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0132","card":"q-sql-053-split-a-column-with-parsename","sec":"sql-s053","q":"How do you store the split OwnerAddress state in a new column?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ALTER TABLE NashvilleHousing\nAdd OwnerSplitState Nvarchar(255);\nUpdate NashvilleHousing\nSET OwnerSplitState = PARSENAME(REPLACE(OwnerAddress, &#x27;,&#x27;, &#x27;.&#x27;) , 1)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0133","card":"q-sql-054-remove-duplicate-records","sec":"sql-s054","q":"How do you find duplicate records with <code>ROW_NUMBER</code>?","a":"<p>Number the rows within each group of identical records. Every row with <code>row_num &gt; 1</code> is a duplicate.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0134","card":"q-sql-054-remove-duplicate-records","sec":"sql-s054","q":"How do you list the duplicate rows of NashvilleHousing?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">SQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>WITH RowNumCTE AS(\nSelect *,\nROW_NUMBER() OVER (\nPARTITION BY ParcelID,\nPropertyAddress,\nSalePrice,\nSaleDate,\nLegalReference\nORDER BY UniqueID) as row_num\nFrom NashvilleHousing\n)\nSelect * From RowNumCTE\nWhere row_num &gt; 1\nOrder by PropertyAddress</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"sql-f0135","card":"q-sql-054-remove-duplicate-records","sec":"sql-s054","q":"How do you remove the duplicates after checking them?","a":"<p>Run the <code>SELECT</code> first to check. Then switch to <code>DELETE</code> to remove them.</p>","hand":true}];
